I ran a few words beginning with 'v' through voc and got the following:

phma@blackcat:~/lojban$ voc vlipa
cid
paur
poder
li
cakt
vlast
phma@blackcat:~/lojban$ voc vraga
No such word
phma@blackcat:~/lojban$ voc vibni
No such word
phma@blackcat:~/lojban$ voc vlagi
rafia
levr
palank
gangan
utolak
ricag

At first I thought "levr" was French "lèvres", which is the descendant of 
"labra" (which I was confusing with "labia"), but French isn't one of the six 
languages, and "palank" sounds a lot more like a piece of wood used as a 
lever than it does a yoni. So it appears that the voc for {vraga} was put in 
{vlagi} by mistake and the voc for {vlagi} omitted. Can anyone else confirm 
or find more errors?

